{number: 157}
{title: I Just Keep Trusting My Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I just keep trusting my Lord as I walk a-[G7] long;
I just keep trusting my Lord, and He gives a [C] song.
Though the storm clouds darken the sky o'er the [F] heav'nly trail,
I just [C] keep on trusting my [G7] Lord, He will never [C] fail.
He's a [F] faithful Friend, such a [C] faithful Friend;
He's a [G7] faithful Friend on whom I can de-[C] pend.
Though the storm clouds darken the sky o'er the [F] heav'nly trail,
I just [C] keep on trusting my [G7] Lord, He will never [C] fail.
{end_of_verse}
